            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Mortgage rates higher, chips rally on OpenAI news, Rivian plunges",
            "description": "<p>Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/alexandra-canal/?fr=sycsrp_catchall\">Allie Canal</a> tracks Thursday's top moving stocks and biggest market stories in this<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-minute/\"> Market Minute</a>.</p>\n<p>Mortgage rates are ticking higher, with the 30-year fixed rate at 6.34%, according to data from Freddie Mac (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/FMCC\">FMCC</a>).</p>\n<p>Chip stocks are rallying, with Nvidia (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NVDA\">NVDA</a>) momentarily touching an intraday high.</p>\n<p>Rivian (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/RIVN\">RIVN</a>) stock is under pressure despite strong delivery numbers last quarter.</p>\n<p>Stay up to date on the latest market action, minute-by-minute, with <a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-minute/\">Yahoo Finance's Market Minute.</a></p>",
